  "adr_0037_n1_6a_criteria_safe_to_check": [
    "Finite binding reserve and exact replay retain one TaskRun and allocate no stream; drift and concurrent replay cannot replace identity.",
    "A finite prefix is a complete takeover anchor before any stream exists; recovery preserves TaskRun identity and normal retry budget without force.",
    "Canonical JSON completion, including null, survives lost response and process/API restart; conflicting completion and corrupted result/outcome witnesses fail closed.",
    "TaskRun success requires the exact receipt; old generation writes and signed events and current signed failures after receipt are rejected before state mutation.",
    "Stream seal requires the exact completed prefix witness; finite tail requires every stream EOF and no in-flight work; Flow success requires prefix/tail receipts and EOF.",
    "Manifest/result quotas, retained release horizon, PostgreSQL/SQLite migration parity and SQLite refusal are exercised against actual storage.",
    "Sync/async clients, client-only DTOs and strict legacy stream-only recovery response compatibility are exercised against actual HTTP and PostgreSQL.",
    "Stream-only, recorder, orchestration, Task/Flow engine, client and lease regressions remain source-bound and green."
  ],
  "adr_0037_n1_6b_criteria_remaining_open": [
    "Ordinary sync and async finite @task invocation around incremental native processing in one mixed @flow.",
    "Stable four-TaskRun/two-channel reconstruction after prefix, document and tail receipt loss.",
    "Runtime skipping of completed prefix/tail and first-incomplete stream replay without re-entering completed user code.",
    "Fail-closed SDK rejection of partial collection, mid-graph finite calls and unsupported finite entrypoints before TaskRun/DATA admission.",
    "Real 500-document mixed-runtime process evidence and production worker launch automation remain separate work."
  ],
  "principal_findings_closed": [
    "Recursive exclude-none was rejected because it deletes an explicit JSON null; unset-only omission preserves legacy strict clients and nested null receipts on initial and exact-replay recovery responses.",
    "Finite receipt authority is attempt-exact. Once accepted, HTTP lifecycle and signed recorder paths reject late failure/retry advancement and only permit exact current Running/Completed reconciliation.",
    "Receipt result size/digest and independently canonical outcome digest are reverified before read, lifecycle, recovery or recorder authority is granted.",
    "Combined finite/stream metadata has a 1 MiB cap, finite results have a 64 KiB cap, release deletes result payload while retaining a named RELEASED manifest horizon.",
    "Prefix-only takeover, exhausted retry rollback, mixed EOF/tail success, direct SQL NULL bypasses and JSON null/signed-zero storage have real PostgreSQL controls."
  ],
